From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6dsp-lpass-clocks: set driver data before registering clocks

Source: https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin/commit/b8fd29b1f39a0cb0d8e8b23c106f5070a9197c1c
Applies after liuqin 7.3.1 refresh/0019; upstream logic retained.
Validation and rollback: tasks/upstream-refresh/RESULT.md.

The prepare and unprepare callbacks look up struct q6dsp_cc through
dev_get_drvdata(), but probe only sets it after the clocks are
registered and the OF provider is added. A consumer that probes in
that window (the LPASS LPI pinctrl resuming through pm_clk) prepares a
clock while the driver data is still NULL and dereferences cc->desc:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0x350
  pc : clk_vote_q6dsp_block+0x24

The fault happens under the clk prepare lock, so every later clock
consumer blocks and the boot never finishes.

Set the driver data before the first clock is registered.

(cherry picked from commit caab65c38df37a835a20ef5e3c88fbf55a83c73c)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

---
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
@@ -146,6 +146,12 @@ int q6dsp_clock_dev_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	cc->dev = dev;
 	q6dsp_clks = desc->clks;
 
+	/*
+	 * The clk ops read the driver data, and a consumer can prepare a
+	 * clock as soon as it is registered, so set it before the first one.
+	 */
+	dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc);
+
 	for (i = 0; i < desc->num_clks; i++) {
 		unsigned int id = q6dsp_clks[i].clk_id;
 		struct clk_init_data init = {
@@ -174,12 +180,6 @@ int q6dsp_clock_dev_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			return ret;
 	}
 
-	ret = devm_of_clk_add_hw_provider(dev, q6dsp_of_clk_hw_get, cc);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-
-	dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc);
-
-	return 0;
+	return devm_of_clk_add_hw_provider(dev, q6dsp_of_clk_hw_get, cc);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(q6dsp_clock_dev_probe);
